        <mxCell id="57oYu3fQP2OPnWM2x2b5-10" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="900" y="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="57oYu3fQP2OPnWM2x2b5-11" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;M&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="820" y="440" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="57oYu3fQP2OPnWM2x2b5-16" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;This ER diagram models the main data structure of the Car Rental System.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;The system contains three core entities: User, Car, and Booking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;A user can create multiple bookings, while each booking belongs to one user. Similarly, one car can appear in multiple bookings over time, while each booking is linked to one car.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;The Bookings entity works as the central transaction record and stores rental details such as rental dates, pickup location, total fee, booking status, and insurance selection.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Primary keys (PK) uniquely identify each record, and foreign keys (FK) in Bookings connect the booking record to the related user and car.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;This structure supports user management, car inventory management, and booking management in the rental system.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="1070" x="190" y="760" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
